SUMMARY:LFS Walk in the Park!
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\nJust a hike around the park\, e
 njoying the weather!\n\nThis event is pet-friendly! Consider bringing wate
 r and snacks. Wear appropriate shoes\, bring water shoes if you would like
  to wade in the river. Sunscreen recommended. Mix of paved trails and dirt
  trails\, some trails might require a moderate climb. The park offers rest
 room facilities. In the event of weather we'll instead meet at Pavilion 1 
 and chat!\n\nAfter crossing the Strawberry St. bridge over the Conestoga r
 iver to enter the park\, there is a parking lot downhill to the left (pict
 ured above). We will meet 9:00am - 9:15am\, pick a route\, and walk!\n\n(I
 f you have difficulty finding the spot on GPS\, try: 38 Pontz Dr\, Lancast
 er\, PA 17602)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-freethought-society/events/
 314836951/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260517T224323Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260517T224323Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Lancaster Freethought Society
UID:event_315144251@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260612T044312Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260613T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260613T173000
SUMMARY:Old School Discussion: Consciousness-Raising Revisited
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\n***Week 3 —* Race\, Class\, a
 nd Community**\n*How do privilege and inequality shape everyday experience
 ?*\n\nWe'll use a short essay by Peggy McIntosh as a starting point and co
 ntinue our format of timed speaking rounds\, attentive listening\, and ref
 lection grounded in lived experience.\nNo homework. No expertise required.
 \n\nIf you'd like to share the details and RSVP:\n[https://www.meetup.com/
 lancaster-freethought-society/events/315144251/](https://www.meetup.com/la
 ncaster-freethought-society/events/315144251/)\n\nThe group remains limite
 d to 10 participants\, so please RSVP if you plan to attend.\nHope to see 
 you there\,\n**Susan**\n\nThis is not therapy\, debate club\, or partisan 
 organizing. It is a structured discussion format built around listening\, 
 reflection\, and lived experience.\nEach session includes:\n\n* 3-minute s
 peaking rounds\n* equal participation\n* the option to pass\n* attentive l
 istening without interruption or debate\n* guided discussion around a week
 ly theme (90 minutes)\n* informal conversation and socializing afterward (
 30 minutes)\n\nFacilitated by Susan Guggenheim\, LFS member.\nAttend one s
 ession or several. Regular attendance is encouraged\, but not required.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-freethought-society/events/
 315144251/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260607T121405Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260607T121405Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
